\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The three-layer architecture. Graph semantics exist only in the top layer; the record store knows nothing about edges or descendants and is reusable for any versioned key--value data; the bottom layer is the public Swarm network. Each layer talks to the next through a narrow interface, so storage-layout changes (chunk packing, batching) never touch graph code.}}{3}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:stack}{{3}{3}{The three-layer architecture. Graph semantics exist only in the top layer; the record store knows nothing about edges or descendants and is reusable for any versioned key--value data; the bottom layer is the public Swarm network. Each layer talks to the next through a narrow interface, so storage-layout changes (chunk packing, batching) never touch graph code}{figure.3}{}}
